WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.534
-Our next guest is an
Emmy-nominated

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.067
comedian and actress
you know from shows such as

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.567
"Nailed It" and "Wipeout."

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.734
She stars in the second season
of "Grand Crew,"

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:09.901
which airs Friday nights
at 8:30 p.m., on NBC.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.067
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.033
-Oh.
Ah, so you're annoyed.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.000
-No, I'm not annoyed.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.534
Um, I think I'm trying to say
that the game is dumb, loud,

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:22.267
and I hate this part
of your personality.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.567
-All right, well, you know what?
The only way to resolve this

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.834
is for you to enter Nebulon 9.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.234
-Oh, no, I don't have time.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.601
-But, Nicole...
-What?

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.601
-...the entire Unified
Intergalactic Tribunal diaspora

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.267
depends on you.
-They definitely don't.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:36.734
-[ Scoffs ]
Just play the game,

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.100
and if you don't like it,
I won't play it

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.400
for as long as I'm here.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.133
-Mm...
-Come on.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:45.300
-Prepare
for intergalactic battle!

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.701
-Please welcome back to the show
the always delightful

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:48.968
Nicole Byer, everybody!

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.467 --> 00:01:00.534
♪♪

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:08.701
♪♪

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.067
Welcome back!
-Thanks for having me.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.567
What a treat.
-I'm so happy to have you

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:13.934
here in person again.
-Yes.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.767
-We've had you on Zoom
a couple of times since.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:18.234
The first time you were here
in 2018 was in person.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.734
And I heard you had
an interesting thing happen

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.033
on your way out the door.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.734
So there was, like,
a bunch of paparazzi,

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:26.000
and I've never encountered that,
and I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.667
[ Giggles ]
And I step out of the car.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.501
And I think J.Lo was
in the building or something

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.400
or, like, Vanessa Hudgens.
Someone famous.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.934
-Yeah.
-And I step out of the car.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.968
I'm with my friend Mateo,
and this little voice,

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.767
little kid goes,
"Mama, who is that?"

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.467
And then the mom goes,
"That's a person."

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:48.133
I'm humbled at every corner.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.968
-To be described as "a person"

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:52.467
is how you know the paparazzi
is not there for you.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.567
-Not for me.
There was like one click.

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.801
Like, a sympathy --
Like, "I don't know."

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.734
-Just in case.
-Yeah, just in case.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:00.868
They're like,
"She might be someone?

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:03.467
She is a person."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:06.834
-Now, I heard you told
a very funny,

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:09.334
a terrible travel story
about a trip to the Bahamas

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.834
on my dear friend
Jimmy Kimmel's show.

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:15.501
-Yeah, and the Bahamas,
they are mad!

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.300
-The Bahamas
has stayed mad at you.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.634
-Yes, this lady took the time --
God bless --

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:22.968
to make a whole video where
she called me Peppa Pig Slut.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:26.267
[ Laughter, groans ]

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:29.200
Someone gasped. It's funny.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.868
-But she took the time
and was that creative.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.200
So I changed
my Twitter bio to that.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.567
-Yeah, you've owned it,
and you changed

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.601
Nicole Byer,
a.k.a. Peppa Pig Slut.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:40.033
So you've taken it from her.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.968
-Yes, I'm reclaiming it.
-Yeah, reclaiming it.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:46.801
And, sadly, though,
not your final bad travel trip.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.467
-No.
-Okay. You had a --

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.133
You had an issue,
and you got into it

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:53.501
maybe a little bit
with the social-media account

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:54.767
of American Airlines.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.567
-American Airlines
is my number-one enemy, okay?

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.234
[ Laughter ]
The whole airline.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.167
Everybody who works there.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.968
I was delayed for eight hours
at the airport.

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:06.133
That's -- That's a
clock-in, clock-out job.

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:08.267
-Yeah.
-I was there for so long.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.601
So, I tweeted, "When are we
getting on this plane?"

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.467
And then some sassy intern
was like,

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.534
"We tried to nail it
with your travel."

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.801
And I was like,
"Don't do puns now!"

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.067
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:20.100
You obviously are on the
fantastic show "Nailed It."

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.634
"Hi, Nicole.
Sorry for the delay.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.701
It's never easy for us.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.868
We always want to nail it
when you travel.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.601
The flight is still scheduled
at 3:00 p.m."

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:28.167
So they probably were
pretty proud of themselves.

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.501
They're like,
"Look at us engaging.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.767
-Yeah, "Ooh, I'm so funny.
Ooh, I love it."

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:33.200
-Yeah.
-"Ha ha ha."

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.734
-You didn't
let them off the hook.

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:36.234
-No.
'Cause they didn't nail it.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.801
I paid $60
to go into the lounge,

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:41.267
and there was toilet paper
all over the bathroom.

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.834
And I posted, I was like,
"Guess you didn't nail this."

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:47.701
-Yeah, this a --
"Ooh, ooh, American Air.

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.601
My flight was supposed
to leave at 7:00 a.m.,

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:50.767
is now leaving at 8:00 p.m.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.834
I paid $60
for your dirty-ass lounge..."

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.100
-"...where barely
any chargers work

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.834
and the bathroom is disgusting.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.467
Guess you didn't nail it again."
-Yeah.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.367
-Now, at this point --
at this point,

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.334
they're definitely regretting
having engaged with you.

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.133
-Oh, I think so.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.934
I absolutely think so.
I wasn't done, though.

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:11.701
I had plenty more to say.
-"A bad joke and you lied.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:15.000
We ain't even on the plane."
-We didn't get on the plane.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.434
And then they canceled
the flight at 5:00 p.m.

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:20.200
-Yeah.
This is -- Now --

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.567
Can I assume these lol's
are sarcastic?

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:23.968
-Oh, yeah.
-Will you read this one for me?

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:28.133
-"Lolol American Airlines,
my flight's canceled!

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.834
Lolololol."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:34.067
"I guess
you really didn't nail it!"

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.767
[ Laughter ]
And that is how I was texting.

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:39.100
I was just
furiously on my iPhone

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.467
just being like, "Aah!"

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:42.801
Ugh. I was so mad.
-Well...

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:44.234
-I was supposed to land
at 1:00 p.m.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:45.801
I didn't land until 6:00 a.m.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.100
and then had to go do
an interview.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.434
I seem drunk in that interview.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:51.100
They were like, "You're on
a show, 'Grand Crew'?"

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.367
And I was like,
"Yeah, you know."

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.334
-And very unfair for them
to treat you like that.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.200
-I know!
I hate them.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.901
If I ever meet the president
of American Airlines,

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:02.534
I'm gonna give them a piece
of my mind and maybe slap him.

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:03.767
-Okay.
I don't know yet.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:04.934
-You don't know yet?

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:06.901
Is there an airline
you would fly instead?

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:09.801
-Listen, I found a piece of poop
in a blanket on Delta.

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.467
Watch my special.
I get into it.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.133
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:14.434
-But I'd rather fly that

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:16.868
because they gave me material
for a show.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:19.634
-Yeah.
-So maybe it's unpleasant,

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:22.234
but they're kind and giving.
You know?

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:24.000
-That's true. A lot of people
don't talk about.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.601
When you get material
on a flight,

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.767
for somebody like you or I...
-Yeah, it's great.

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:28.868
-...you know, we're being
enriched by that.

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:33.000
-Yes.
-You obviously are from Chicago.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.467
Not obviously,
but you're from Chicago.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.934
And I heard, one holiday,
you could not get home.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:39.834
And a family member did a very
sweet thing to make you feel --

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.434
they tried to bring
the holidays to you.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.801
-Yes, my aunt.
What a sweet, sweet woman.

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:47.701
She said, "I'm gonna send you
Easter dinner via the mail."

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:50.400
And my sweet aunt --
-Now, did you think

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.634
when you heard that
there was maybe problem brewing?

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:57.200
-Well, I was like, "Surely, it's
stuff I have to make on my own.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.200
She's not gonna make me dinner."
-Yeah, that's true.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.334
There's a lot of canned goods
at Easter, right.

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:03.567
-But I was wrong.
-Okay.

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:06.567
-She made, like, a ham.
There was -- [ Laughs ]

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.801
There was unrefrigerated bacon.
-Okay.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.901
-And I was like, "Who's
eating bacon at dinner?"

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:12.801
It just wasn't thought-out.
-Uh-huh.

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:15.267
-So, it gets to the Post Office
after being on the truck

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:16.434
for such a long time.

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.300
The Post Office is closed
due to the holiday.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.367
-Sure, that makes sense.
-I get to the Post Office.

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:22.934
Two postal workers are like,
"Oh, my gosh, she's here!"

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:26.534
And I was like, "She's here?"
Truly, the box is dripping.

00:06:26.534 --> 00:06:28.667
It's like the box
at the end of "Se7en."

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:32.334
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:34.300
And it stinks.
It's like, "What is in the box?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.767
What is in the box?!"

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.501
-So they were excited
to see what was in the box?

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:38.934
-Yes, this is the talk
of the week.

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:41.100
This stinky box
belonged to this woman.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.534
-I have met --
You know what?

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:45.067
Of all the different reactions
postal employees could have

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:46.734
to a stinky box,
I'm kind of excited

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:48.067
they treated it
like a game show.

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:49.400
[ Laughter ]
-Me too.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.534
'Cause they could've
yelled at me and been like,

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.968
"What is this?!"
And I'd be like, "I don't know."

00:06:52.968 --> 00:06:56.000
I pulled out a full ham.
It was wild.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.334
It must have been so
anti-climactic for them.

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:00.634
They were like "Oh, my God.
It's a body, it's something."

00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:01.968
It's like,
"No, it's just old ham."

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:04.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:06.601
-That's true. But at least that
way they're not witnesses.

00:07:06.601 --> 00:07:08.167
You know, you probably
have to file a police report

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:10.234
if you find a body in a box.
-It's the Post Office.

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:13.067
They weren't gonna do anything.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:14.267
I once filed a complaint.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.634
I was like,
"I didn't get my package."

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:17.400
Two days later, they were like,
"We hope you got it."

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.133
I was like...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:21.634
..."You didn't do anything."

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:23.133
-They're like,
"Well, maybe it'll come."

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:24.634
-"Maybe it'll come.
Who knows?"

00:07:24.634 --> 00:07:25.834
They were like,
"Contact the sender,"

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:29.467
and I was like, "What?"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:31.767
-Now, I do want to --
the clip that you showed

00:07:31.767 --> 00:07:33.567
when you walked out here --
this is a very funny show.

00:07:33.567 --> 00:07:34.968
Colton Dunn, one of my --

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:36.334
I've known Colton
for like 20 years.

00:07:36.334 --> 00:07:37.934
-He's the best.
-It's a fantastic cast.

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:39.300
Do you enjoy working with
everybody over there

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.934
on that show?
-Oh, God, I love it so much.

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:43.501
I've known everyone for so long.
The creator I've known

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.400
since we were, like,
improvising in New York

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.834
under Gristedes with, like,
[bleep ] dripping on us.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:49.667
-Yeah, there you go -- UCB.
-Yeah, UCB.

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:52.334
Oh, God bless.
And, truly, like,

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:55.868
everyone is so fun and so great.
Colton is just, like, amazing.

00:07:55.868 --> 00:07:57.100
[ Valley girl voice ]
It's like going to work with,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.000
like, my friends,
and it's, like, not even a job.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:02.267
-Well, I feel like, for a lot of
people that work with you,

00:08:02.267 --> 00:08:04.300
and I know this isn't
the only show you do,

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.601
I would imagine
working with Nicole Byer

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:06.801
almost never feels like a job.
-Oh.

00:08:06.801 --> 00:08:08.267
-Is that what you
try to bring to a project?

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:10.267
-Listen, if I'm not having fun,
we go home.

00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:11.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.634 --> 00:08:13.767
-I think that's a good way
to approach this profession.

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:15.033
-What's the point
in not having fun?

00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:16.634
It's like,
"I'mma cash that check,

00:08:16.634 --> 00:08:18.300
but I'mma have fun doing it."
-There you go.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.767
And I think
nobody would complain

00:08:19.767 --> 00:08:21.534
about you doing
both of those things.

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:23.167
And it's always such a delight
to have you here.

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:24.400
Thank you so much
for coming back.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.801
-Thank you for having me.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:25.801 --> 00:08:28.133
-You guys, the one,
the only Nicole Byer.

00:08:28.133 --> 00:08:30.901
"Grand Crew" airs Friday nights
at 8:30 p.m. here on NBC.

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:33.801
We'll be right back with
a performance from Keshi.

